---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base title="Colophon" description="How this site is built, and the decisions behind it.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <p class="lede">How this site is put together, written the same way as the rest: what I chose, and what it cost.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose cv">
    <h2>Static pages</h2>
    <p>
      Every post and every DSA note is its own plain HTML page, built with
      Astro. Search engines and people with JavaScript off get exactly what
      everyone else gets. The cost: publishing means rebuilding, which takes
      about three seconds, so I’ll allow it.
    </p>

    <h2>Notes from the vault</h2>
    <p>
      The DSA notes live in my Obsidian vault, and the build reads them
      straight from there. Wikilinks turn into real links, Obsidian-only
      blocks get dropped. I never copy a note into this repo, which also means
      the site can’t build without the vault sitting next to it.
    </p>

    <h2>Borrowed looks</h2>
    <p>
      The colours, the Nunito type and the little ledge under every button come
      from my apps, <a href="https://github.com/Navknight/rituals">Rituals</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Navknight/tally">Tally</a>. Diagram labels and code
      are set in <a href="https://commitmono.com">Commit Mono</a>. The diagrams
      are hand-placed SVG, so moving a box means editing coordinates. Worth it.
    </p>

    <h2>Very little JavaScript</h2>
    <p>
      Scripts handle the theme switch, search, the clock in the corner, the
      problem filter and the lab games. Nothing fades in as you scroll, and
      there’s one stylesheet and no framework.
    </p>

    <h2>No tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No analytics, no cookies. The only thing stored is your light or dark
      choice, in your own browser. I have no idea if you’re reading this, which
      is honestly a bit freeing.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages. The source is on <a href="https://github.com/Navknight/navknight.github.io">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
